<title>JAPAN: Japan April/Sept crude imports fall 1.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan April/Sept crude imports fall 1.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's imports of crude oil in six months from April to September totalled 124 million kilolitres (kl), down 1.8 percent compared with the same period a year earlier, the Trade Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>The amount of crude processed during the six months was 115 million kl, up 1.2 percent year-on-year, the Ministry said.</p>
<p>Details on crude imports were as follows:</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL   (1,000 kl) (1,000 bbl) yr/yr%</p>
<p> Iran	   11,201	 70,454   +12.1</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia 23,747	149,369   - 2.3</p>
<p> Kuwait	  6,393	 40,212   + 6.2</p>
<p> Neutral Zone  6,527	 41,055   -10.8</p>
<p> Qatar	   8,772	 55,176   +11.5</p>
<p> Oman	    6,546	 41,174   -20.4</p>
<p> UAE	    34,395	216,345   + 1.8</p>
<p> China	   6,744	 42,420   - 0.1</p>
<p> Indonesia     8,867	 55,773   -14.7</p>
<p> Mexico	  2,525	 15,882   + 0.6</p>
<p> Others	  8,356	 52,559    -9.0</p>
<p> TOTAL	 124,071	780,407    -1.8</p>
</text>
